# mutgap_mem_tracker_remove_search: RunBlock::remove's binary search can stop on a run after the one that contains the removed range, and the scan from there then never sees it. Runs [0,1), [4,5), [8,12) and [16,17); an unmap of page 10: the search ends at index 3 ([16,17), which compares Greater and is skipped), so [8,12) is not split and the tracker still counts page 10 as mapped, although the host was asked to unmap it. A probe of page 10 then asks the host to map nothing; a probe of page 12, never mapped, maps it.
